  "aiContextParagraph": "The Malaysian judiciary recently authorized the transfer of former Prime Minister Najib Razak from prison to house arrest, a decision tied to his ongoing legal proceedings related to the 1MDB corruption scandal. This development prompted an immediate resignation from the Minister of Transport, Anthony Loke. Following the court's issuance of a new warrant, the former leader has since arrived at his private residence in Taman Duta to begin his confinement. While he has been granted this transition, reports indicate that he faces additional outstanding legal challenges, including a separate 15-year prison sentence. Furthermore, government sources have confirmed that specific restrictions are in place regarding his living arrangements, stating that individuals such as his wife, Rosmah Mansor, will not be allowed to live with him during the duration of his house arrest.",
